<title>USA: Ryder expects Q4 charge for cost reductions.</title>
<headline>Ryder expects Q4 charge for cost reductions.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ryder System Inc said Monday that it expects to take a charge in the fourth quarter for cost reductions related to its voluntary retirement program.</p>
<p>The company offered a voluntary retirement program to U.S. hourly and salaried employees of Ryder System and Ryder Transportation Services.  </p>
<p>Ryder said that retirement dates for employees who elect to participate will be January 1, February 1 or March 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Employees who elect to take the voluntary retirement program receive a pension benefit enhanced by an additional three years added to the employee's age and three years added to the employee's service with the company.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
